                <ul><h2 style="color:coral;">Part-2: CSS</h2>
                    <div>
                        <li><h2>Selectors in CSS</h2>
                            <ul>
                                <li><b>Universal Selector:</b>
                                    <p>To select everything in the document.</p>
                                    <p>
                                        * {
                                            property:value;
                                        }
                                        where '*' is the universal selector.
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                                <li><b>Element Selector:</b>
                                    <p>Select all elements of the same type.</p>
                                    <p>
                                        h1 {
                                            property:value;
                                        }
                                        where 'h1' is the element selector.
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                                <li><b>ID Selector:</b>
                                    <p>Select an element based on the value of the elements id alternative.</p>
                                    <p>
                                        #myId {
                                            property:value;
                                        }
                                        where 'myId' is the id selector and always remember to put '#' ahead of any id selector.
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                                <li><b>Class Selector:</b>
                                    <p>Selects an element based on their class attribute.</p>
                                    <p>
                                        .myclass {
                                            property:value;
                                        }
                                        where 'myclass' is the class selector and always remember to put '.' ahead of any class selector.
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                                <li><b>Descendent Selector</b>
                                    <p>Selects all paragraphs inside divs.</p>
                                    <p>
                                        div p {
                                            property:value;
                                        }
                                        where 'div p' is the desecendent selector and always remember to have gap in between.
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                                <li><b>Sibling Combinator:</b>
                                    <p>Heading 3 that comes immediately after any paragraph.</p>
                                    <p>
                                        p + h3 {
                                           property:value; 
                                        }
                                        where '+' is the sibling combinator.
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                                <li><b>Child Combinator:</b>
                                    <p>Selects all buttons within which are direct children of spans.</p>
                                    <p>
                                        span > button {
                                            property: value;
                                        }
                                        where '>' is the child combinator.
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                                <li><b>Attribute Selector:</b>
                                    <p>Selects element based on the presence or value of a given attribute.</p>
                                    <p>
                                        input [attr = "value"] {
                                            property: value;
                                        }
                                        where input [attr = "-"] is the attribute selector.
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li><h2>Pseudo Class:</h2>
                            <p>A keyword added to a selector that specifies a special state of the selected element(s).</p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>:hover</li>
                                <li>:active</li>
                                <li>:checked</li>
                                <li>:nth-of-type</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li><h2>Pseudo Element:</h2>
                            <p>A keyword added to a selector that lets you style a specified part of the selected elements.</p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>::first-letter</li>
                                <li>::first-line</li>
                                <li>::selection</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <li><h2>CSS:Cascading Style Sheets:</h2>
                            <p><b>Cascade in CSS:</b>The CSS cascade algorithm's job is to select CSS declaration in order<br>
                            to determine the correct values for CSS properties. (For same selector)</p>
                            <h3>Selector Specificity (for different selector):</h3>
                            <p>An algorithm that calculates the weight that is applied to given CSS declaration.</p>
                            <p>_____ id ________ class, attribute and pseudo-class ________ element and pseudo element</p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>id>class>element</li>
                                <li>more sector ^ CSS > less sector</li>
                                <li>if specificity is the same, we check cascading.</li>
                            </ul>
                            <h3>Inline Specificity:</h3>
                            <p>Inline Styles are more specific than id.</p>
                            <p>_____ inline style _______ id ______ class, attribute and pseudo-class ________ element and pseudo element</p>
                        </li>
